# Verified on a real Debian 13 (trixie) box via `dpkg-buildpackage -us
# -uc -b`: dh_shlibdeps resolves ${shlibs:Depends} for libfuzzy-dev
# (ssdeep) fine despite it not shipping a pkg-config file (it still
# carries proper shlibs metadata) - computed deps came out as
# libfuzzy2, libyara10, libnl-genl-3-200, no manual Depends: needed.
# TLSH fuzzy hashing needs no such entry at all: it's vendored, pure C
# (userspace/avd/tlsh_core.c/.h), not linked against a system libtlsh.
Source: hyprav
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: keanehatescoding <159132270+keanehatescoding@users.noreply.github.com>
# python3-gi/gir1.2-gtk-4.0 are needed at build time, not just runtime:
# userspace/av-gui/Makefile's `install` target depends on `checkdeps`
# (imports gi, loads GTK4). Missing on a clean builder, this fails the
# build before av-gui ever gets installed - only worked on the Debian
# 13 test box because those happened to already be present there.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               dh-sequence-installsysusers,
               pkg-config,
               libnl-genl-3-dev,
               libyara-dev,
               libfuzzy-dev,
               python3,
               python3-gi,
               gir1.2-gtk-4.0
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/keanehatescoding/antivirus
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: hyprav-dkms
Architecture: amd64
Depends: dkms, ${misc:Depends}
Description: HyprAV kprobe-based execve/file-event kernel module (DKMS)
 Out-of-tree kernel module (av.ko) that hooks execve and file events via
 kprobes, does fast hash/counter checks in-kernel, and talks to the avd
 userspace daemon over netlink for anything heavier (YARA, entropy,
 fuzzy hashing). Ships as DKMS source and is rebuilt automatically
 against every installed kernel.
 .
 x86_64 only as shipped - the module hooks __x64_sys_execve by symbol
 name; arm64 needs source changes to hook __arm64_sys_execve instead.

Package: hyprav
Architecture: amd64
# pkexec, not policykit-1: the latter no longer exists as an
# installable package on Debian 13/trixie (confirmed - `apt install
# policykit-1` fails with "Depends: policykit-1 but it is not
# installable"). pkexec is the actual binary avctl invokes
# (`pkexec avctl ...`); it split into its own package from the old
# monolithic policykit-1 and depends on polkitd itself, so this pulls
# in everything actually needed.
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, pkexec
Recommends: hyprav-dkms
Description: HyprAV userspace scanning daemon and control CLI
 avd is the privileged userspace daemon that the av.ko kernel module
 defers heavyweight checks to: YARA matching, ELF structural analysis,
 entropy scoring, ssdeep/TLSH fuzzy hashing, and quarantine
 (move + chmod 0000) of anything avd itself flags. avctl is the CLI
 (and polkit-gated privileged entry point) for managing avd's
 signatures, trust list, protected paths, policy, on-demand scans, and
 quarantine.
 .
 avd fails fast and keeps retrying if av.ko (from hyprav-dkms) isn't
 loaded yet - install that package too for the kernel-level
 execve/file interception this project is built around.

Package: hyprav-gui
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, hyprav (= ${binary:Version})
Description: GTK4 management console for HyprAV
 Dashboard (avd status + counts), detections (recent verdict history),
 quarantine (list/restore/delete), an on-demand scan page, and
 signatures/trust list/protected paths/policy management, sitting on
 top of avd and avctl. A normal desktop app, not a daemon - nothing to
 enable or start, just launch it. Privileged actions go through
 pkexec avctl, gated by the per-verb org.hyprav.avctl.* polkit actions
 installed by the hyprav package.
